#
# Frozen 2026-08-15, on publication of lnzip.de.
#
# Once a line appears here it is permanent. A model id names the statistics a
# payload was coded against, so a link minted under id 0 only decodes correctly
# under id 0 — for as long as that link exists, which is forever. A published
# model is therefore never re-edited and its id is never reassigned; a retrain
# gets a new id and the old file stays distributed.
#
# The model files themselves are release assets, not source: they are ten
# megabytes each, which does not belong in a git history. The hashes belong
# here, in the repository, because a link whose model was lost is a dead link
# and the hash is what proves a recovered copy is the right one.
#
# BOTH WERE TRAINED ON PUBLIC DATA, and that is a requirement rather than a
# convenience. A dictionary holds the tokens its corpus contained, so a model
# trained on someone's browsing would publish their searches. These were
# trained on 27 million URLs from a Common Crawl index filtered to English and
# Portuguese, with a floor of eight sightings before any token may enter a
# dictionary, and the host dictionary seeded from a public popularity list.
